
+ Make the server awesome:
    + Make Server.join_room() validate names.
    + Make Server.create_room() validate names.
    + Make Server.create_room() validate board sizes.
        - Otherwise it's vulnerable to an attack where you just request a huge board that would use up all of RAM.
    + Remove as many trait bounds as possible from the Game trait.
    + Separate Server out into its own crate.
    + Make the server delete any socket that hasn't had activity in, say, an hour.
    + Make the PlayerJoined info message announce the role of the new player.

+ Make the game awesome:
    + Make there be a 1/100 chance that a stone is textured with the stare emoji (not in the first ~5 moves so as not to be confusing).
    + Add a GameHistory class.

+ Write tests for the web app?
    - Host can't play until player arrives.
    - Frame all tests in terms of the actions of *clients* (i.e. WebSocket connections).
      These clients can do things like create accounts, take actions with those accounts
      (by providing the API-given credential), and maybe other things? But ultimately
      they are the things that the server deals with.
    - Same user can have multiple clients and they all work.

+ Write a bunch of insta tests.
    - Wins.
    - Double wins.
    - Multiple wins for same player.
    - Correct rotation of numbers.
    - Correct position of numbers.
    - Stalemate.
    - Win averted if the spin ruins it.
    - Every error condition under the sun.

